<title>BELGIUM: Fischler rejects Irish call for higher ewe premium.</title>
<headline>Fischler rejects Irish call for higher ewe premium.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler rejected an Irish request to raise the ewe premium paid to farmers, a Commission official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Ireland expected prices to be same throughout the EU but it was up to the Irish sheepmeat industry to raise prices, the official said.</p>
<p>EU sheepmeat prices have risen 28 percent since shoppers switched away from beef following the outbreak of the mad cow disease crisis in March, according to the Commission.</p>
</text>
